{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.self_duality_and_eightfold_exclusive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.self_duality_and_eightfold_exclusive","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L178-L181","doc":"Stated as the consequence that matters: fixing the rank disagreement does\n**not** open the eightfold route. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.three_requirements_pairwise_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.three_requirements_pairwise_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L170-L176","doc":"**The three-way collision.**  No contact manifold satisfies two of the three\nrequirements — so resolving the rank-2-vs-rank-4 disagreement in *either*\ndirection leaves the eightfold route closed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.bringDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.bringDim","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L167-L168","doc":"Bring's worked example. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.selfDualityDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.selfDualityDim","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L164-L165","doc":"The dimension self-duality requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.eightfoldDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.eightfoldDim","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L160-L162","doc":"The dimension the eightfold way requires, from\n`ContactDistributionRank.complexRank_three_iff_dim_seven`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.woronowicz_three_star_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.woronowicz_three_star_target","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L157-L158","doc":"The Woronowicz 3-dimensional calculus sends `Ω²` to `Ω¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.categorical_star_needs_calculus_dim_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.categorical_star_needs_calculus_dim_four","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L150-L155","doc":"**The categorical mismatch.**  `⋆_q : Ω^k(A) → Ω^{n−k}(A)` is an involution\n*on `Ω²`* only at calculus dimension 4; the declared Woronowicz left-covariant\ncalculus has dimension 3, where `⋆` maps `Ω²` to `Ω¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.rank_four_extSquare_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.rank_four_extSquare_dim","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L146-L148","doc":"At `n = 2` it is six-dimensional, which is what splits `3 + 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.bring_extSquare_is_a_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.bring_extSquare_is_a_line","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L141-L144","doc":"And the exterior square is a line there, not a six-dimensional space with\nroom to split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.bring_dim_admits_no_splitting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.bring_dim_admits_no_splitting","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L135-L139","doc":"**Bring's `M_S` admits no splitting.**  At `dim M_S = 3` the distribution has\nreal rank 2 and `Λ²H^*` is one-dimensional — `⋆` maps it to `Λ⁰`, so there is no\nendomorphism and no `Λ^±`.  Hence `F_A^+` does not exist at that dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.splitting_forces_dim_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.splitting_forces_dim_five","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L130-L133","doc":"…equivalently, `dim M = 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.splitting_forces_n_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.splitting_forces_n_two","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L121-L128","doc":"**`Λ^±H^*` forces CR dimension `n = 2`, hence `dim M = 5`.**  This is the\ncontent of `archimedean-realisations.md:3`'s rank-4 claim: it is not an\nassertion but the hypothesis under which the corpus's own simplicity constraint\n`B ∈ Γ(Λ^+H^* ⊗ Ad(P))` is well-formed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.crDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.crDim","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L118-L119","doc":"The dimension of the CR manifold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.distributionRealRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.distributionRealRank","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L115-L116","doc":"The real rank of the contact distribution of a `(2n+1)`-manifold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.selfDual_two_forms_iff_dim_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.selfDual_two_forms_iff_dim_four","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L109-L113","doc":"**Self-duality of 2-forms exists in dimension 4 and nowhere else.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.hodgeTarget_eq_self_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.hodgeTarget_eq_self_iff","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**The endomorphism criterion.**  `⋆ : Λ^k → Λ^{m−k}` is an endomorphism of\n`Λ^k` — hence can carry a `±1` eigenspace splitting — exactly when `m = 2k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.hodgeTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualityDegree.hodgeTarget","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualityDegree.lean#L99-L100","doc":"The degree the Hodge star sends `Λ^k` to, on an `m`-dimensional space. ","signatureChunk":0}]}